## Worktrees

All implementation work happens in a dedicated worktree — never on the
main checkout. The PreToolUse hook enforces this and the BLOCKED message
points at the canonical one-command path.

```bash
# Register task state and post intent for an existing issue
# (idempotent: re-run the same command to re-post intent and re-enter the worktree)
eval "$(holly task start --id <issue-id> --intent '<agent-intent>')"

# Where am I, what's next? (current task — NOT whole-project status)
holly task status

# Re-cd into the active worktree (e.g. after a shell reset)
eval "$(holly task resume)"

# When work in the worktree is committed
eval "$(holly task finish)"

# Wrong issue / give up — refuses unpushed commits unless --force
eval "$(holly task abort)"
```

**Safety contract.** `start` requires the existing shell/runtime-owned
`HOLLY_SESSION_ID`, records task ID and/or intent in session state, and posts
intent to all-agents in the same step. Re-running `start` with the same active
id is idempotent: it re-posts intent and re-enters the worktree without
re-claiming or recreating it.
The active adapter's worktree tool owns checkout creation; use the BLOCKED
message or `holly worktree ...` pass-through for adapter-specific worktree
operations. `finish` resolves the integration branch via `origin/HEAD` then
`main`/`master`/`trunk`/`develop`, **verifies the main checkout is on that
branch and clean** before the FF-merge, then pushes when a remote exists,
closes the issue, syncs tracker state, removes the worktree, and clears the
session. `abort` is the symmetric give-up: refuses to discard unpushed work
without `--force`, removes the worktree, reopens the issue, clears the session.
If no `worktree_path` is registered, `finish` is a summary-only recovery path:
it can post the lifecycle summary, but it does not push, close, sync, remove a
worktree, or clear task state. Do not wrap that no-worktree recovery path in
`eval`.

**Output.** All eval-emitting verbs (`start`, `finish`, `abort`, `resume`) take
`--json` for non-eval consumers and print a one-line `eval` reminder to stderr
if you forget the `eval` wrapper (detected via `stdout.isatty()`).

`holly task start` is adapter-agnostic session/task registration. Worktree
operations are adapter-aware through `holly worktree ...`, which passes through
to the native tracker worktree command when the active adapter exposes one.

See `docs/worktree-workflow.md` for the full lifecycle.

